  "articleBody": "A bedroom addition usually requires more than framing a new room: the project must be designed around the existing structure, permitted through the appropriate local jurisdiction, and planned for light, ventilation, emergency escape, alarms, electrical service, and heating or cooling. Cost changes with size, foundation and soil conditions, roof connections, finish choices, plumbing, site constraints, and permit complexity.",
